  "formula": {
    "tex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\term{observedStandardDeviation}{s_k}&=\\operatorname{sd}_i\\,\\beta_{ik},\n&\\term{simulatedMean}{\\bar s_k}&=\\frac{1}{P}\\sum_{p=1}^{P}s_k^{(p)}\\\\\n\\term{exceedances}{g_k}&=\\#\\{p:\\ s_k^{(p)}\\ge s_k\\},\n&\\term{pseudoPValue}{p_k}&=\\frac{g_k+1}{\\term{permutationCount}{P}+1}\\\\\n\\term{zSimulated}{z_k}&=\\frac{s_k-\\bar s_k}{\\term{simulatedDeviation}{\\sigma_{s_k}}}\n\\end{aligned}",
    "ascii": "s_k = population standard deviation of the local estimates beta_ik over the tracts with a finite fit. Permutation p relabels (X, y) among the tracts with a keyed swap-or-not shuffle, refits every tract at the bandwidth already selected on the observed data, and records s_k^(p). g_k = number of permutations with s_k^(p) >= s_k; pseudo p = (g_k + 1)/(P + 1); z_k = (s_k - mean of s_k^(p))/sd of s_k^(p). Failed permuted fits are left out and counted.",
